# FactsPack artifacts are byte-sensitive: real tabs as field separators,
# LF (0x0A) as the record separator per FACTSPACK.md §4. Never let git
# convert their line endings.
*.pack text eol=lf
*.pack-diff text eol=lf

# Everything else: normalize to LF and CHECK OUT as LF on every platform. This
# repo is byte-sensitive end to end — the vendored codec bundle
# (test/factspack.bundle.mjs) and the inlined encoder in docs/index.html are
# compared byte-for-byte against a fresh LF esbuild by the INLINE-DRIFT /
# BUNDLE-DRIFT guards, so a CRLF checkout (autocrlf on Windows) would make those
# guards false-fail. Pinning eol=lf keeps a clean clone byte-identical everywhere.
* text=auto eol=lf
